WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:02.630
- [Narrator] This is kakigori.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.300
It's a traditional
Japanese dessert similar

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.400
to the shaved ice desserts
that you probably know.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.483
But of course, here, it
is so much more than that.

00:00:12.553 --> 00:00:15.053
(happy music)

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.000
Let's start with a quick history.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.710
The dish was originally a
summer treat meant to help

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.335
cool down the wealthy elite of
Japan during the late 1800s.

00:00:25.335 --> 00:00:29.100
The ice was topped with
fruit syrups and teas grown

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.116
and harvested locally, and,
in some places, it still is.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:37.353
This is Aya Eguchi in her shop in Otsu.

00:01:09.957 --> 00:01:11.340
- [Narrator] And to get very thin ice,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.810
there is, of course, a
special machine for that,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.975
which you can find in
Tokyo at Kori Ishibashi.

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:20.133
This is Kumiko Ishibashi in her shop.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.330
- [Narrator] How thin the ice is shaved?

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.293
Well, that depends on the weather.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.820
- [Narrator] OK, so we've
got our pure non-freezer

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:50.510
made ice shaved by hand to
perfection based on the weather.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.260
Next, we need toppings.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.670
Our last stop is Chasanraku
tea house in Kyoto.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.900
An area known for its matcha.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.177
And this is Hiroki.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.530
- [Narrator] From more
traditional matcha flavors

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.450
to mainstream ones like strawberry,

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.860
Hawaii blue, melon, cream.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.532
This dish has range.

00:02:25.532 --> 00:02:28.495
But the only thing that
matters at the end of the day

00:02:28.495 --> 00:02:31.283
is how delicious it is.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.950
(upbeat music)

